1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,700
Section 2

2
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:03,186
Thanks for coming everyone.

3
00:00:03,186 --> 00:00:03,874
OK,

4
00:00:03,874 --> 00:00:09,961
so this meeting is for new staff and staff who haven't been involved with

5
00:00:09,961 --> 00:00:11,700
our volunteering projects yet.

6
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:17,050
So basically, the idea is that we allow staff to give up some of

7
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:22,400
their work time to help on various charity projects to benefit the local community.

8
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:27,300
We've been doing this for the last five years and it's been very successful.

9
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:31,211
Participating doesn't necessarily involve a huge time commitment.

10
00:00:31,211 --> 00:00:36,100
The company will pay for eight hours of your time.

11
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:41,080
That can be used over one or two days all at once,

12
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:44,400
or spread over several months throughout the year.

13
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:49,358
There are some staff who enjoy volunteering so much they also give up their

14
00:00:49,358 --> 00:00:52,900
own free time for a couple of hours every week.

15
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:55,281
It's completely up to you.

16
00:00:55,281 --> 00:01:01,948
Obviously, many people will have family commitments and aren't as available as other members

17
00:01:01,948 --> 00:01:02,900
of staff.

18
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:06,900
Feedback from staff has been overwhelmingly positive.

19
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:13,033
Because they felt they were doing something really useful, nearly everyone agreed that volunteering

20
00:01:13,033 --> 00:01:16,100
made them feel more motivated at work.

21
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:20,427
They also liked building relationships with the people in the local community

22
00:01:20,427 --> 00:01:22,230
and felt valued by them.

23
00:01:22,230 --> 00:01:27,279
One or two people also said it was a good thing to have on

24
00:01:27,279 --> 00:01:28,000
their CVs.

25
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:34,400
One particularly successful project last year was the Get Working Project.

26
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:39,400
This was aimed at helping unemployed people in the area get back to work.

27
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:46,517
Our staff were able to help them improve their telephone skills, such as writing down messages

28
00:01:46,517 --> 00:01:49,631
and speaking with confidence to potential customers,

29
00:01:49,631 --> 00:01:52,300
which they had found quite difficult.

30
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:56,387
This is something many employers look for in job applicants -

31
00:01:56,387 --> 00:02:01,700
and something we all do without even thinking about, every day at work.

32
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:04,987
We've got an exciting new project starting this year.

33
00:02:04,987 --> 00:02:10,100
Up until now, we've mainly focused on projects to do with education and training.

34
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:15,793
And we'll continue with our reading project in schools and our work with local

35
00:02:15,793 --> 00:02:16,200
charities.

36
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:22,800
But we've also agreed to help out on a conservation project in Redfern Park.

37
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:27,958
So if any of you fancy being outside and getting your hands dirty, this

38
00:02:27,958 --> 00:02:29,800
is the project for you.

39
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:33,559
I also want to mention the annual Digital Inclusion Day,

40
00:02:33,559 --> 00:02:35,814
which is coming up next month.

41
00:02:35,814 --> 00:02:40,700
The aim of this is to help older people keep up with technology.

42
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:46,100
And this year, instead of hosting the event in our own training facility, we're

43
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:51,500
using the ICT suite at Hill College, as it can hold far more people.

44
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:56,454
We've invited over 60 people from the Silver Age Community Centre to take part,

45
00:02:56,454 --> 00:03:00,700
so we'll need a lot of volunteers to help with this event.

46
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:06,550
If you're interested in taking part, please go to the volunteering section of our website

47
00:03:06,550 --> 00:03:08,500
and complete the relevant form.

48
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:13,845
We won't be providing any training for this but you'll be paired with an

49
00:03:13,845 --> 00:03:16,900
experienced volunteer if you've never done it before.

50
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:23,159
By the way, don't forget to tell your manager about any volunteering activities you

51
00:03:23,159 --> 00:03:24,500
decide to do.

52
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:28,033
The participants on the Digital Inclusion Day really benefited.

53
00:03:28,033 --> 00:03:31,959
The majority were in their seventies, though some were younger

54
00:03:31,959 --> 00:03:35,100
and a few were even in their nineties!

55
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:39,500
Quite a few owned both a computer and a mobile phone,

56
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:42,300
but these tended to be outdated models.

57
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:45,810
They generally knew how to do simple things, like send texts,

58
00:03:45,810 --> 00:03:49,000
but weren't aware of recent developments in mobile phone technology.

59
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:55,350
A few were keen to learn but most were quite dismissive at first -

60
00:03:55,350 --> 00:03:59,746
they couldn't see the point of updating their skills.

61
00:03:59,746 --> 00:04:01,700
But that soon changed.

62
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:04,600
The feedback was very positive.

63
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:10,317
The really encouraging thing was that participants all said they felt much more confident

64
00:04:10,317 --> 00:04:14,808
about using social media to keep in touch with their grandchildren,

65
00:04:14,808 --> 00:04:19,300
who prefer this form of communication to phoning or sending emails.

66
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:24,625
A lot of them also said playing online games would help them make new friends

67
00:04:24,625 --> 00:04:26,400
and keep their brains active.

68
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:31,226
They weren't that impressed with being able to order their groceries online, as they

69
00:04:31,226 --> 00:04:33,295
liked going out to the shops,

70
00:04:33,295 --> 00:04:37,432
but some said it would come in handy if they were ill

71
00:04:37,432 --> 00:04:39,500
or the weather was really bad.

72
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:44,736
One thing they asked about was using tablets for things like reading newspapers -

73
00:04:44,736 --> 00:04:49,972
some people had been given tablets as presents but had never used them,

74
00:04:49,972 --> 00:04:54,000
so that's something we'll make sure we include this time ...
